Need animation loop. We'll maintain `mode` and `characters` array.

Let's create helper to clear dynamic objects: group `stageGroup` for runway characters; we can remove.

Character creation function:

```js
function createCharacter(species, outfit) {
  const group = new THREE.Group();
  const skinColor = species==='goblin' ? 0x4caf50 : 0x8d6e63;
  const mat = (c, opts={}) => new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({color:c, roughness:0.7, ...opts});
  // torso
  const torso = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.35,0.4,0.85,12), mat(skinColor));
  torso.position.y = 1.0; 
  if (species==='goblin') torso.rotation.x = 0.18;
  group.add(torso);
  // head
  const head = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.32,16,16), mat(skinColor));
  head.position.y = 1.65; 
  if (species==='goblin') { head.position.y=1.6; head.scale.set(1.05,0.95,1.05); }
  group.add(head);
  // neck
  ...
  // arms
  function limb(x, yTop, color) {
    const upper = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.1,0.11,0.45,8), mat(color));
    upper.position.set(x, yTop-0.22, 0); group.add(upper);
    const lower = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.09,0.1,0.4,8), mat(color));
    lower.position.set(x, yTop-0.62, 0); group.add(lower);
    const hand = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.1,8,8), mat(color));
    hand.position.set(x, yTop-0.85,0); group.add(hand);
  }
  limb(-0.48,1.35,skinColor); limb(0.48,1.35,skinColor);
  // legs
  limb(-0.18,0.62,skinColor? but pants color); etc. Need separate.
```

This is getting complex. Let's simplify character: use capsule-like cylinders; clothing colors applied to regions.

Maybe create base body with arrays of meshes and store references to apply colors:
- torsoMesh (skin)
- headMesh
- leftArm meshes, rightArm
- leftLeg meshes, rightLeg
- feet meshes

Then clothing:
- Top: create a cylinder over torso with item color (slightly larger radius) and add.
- Pants: color leg meshes with pants color (instead of skin) or add cylinder.
- Socks: lower leg color.
- Shoes: feet color.
- Underwear: hip cylinder color.
- Hat: mesh on head.
- Glasses: two small cylinders/torus in front of eyes.
- Accessories: necklace torus.
- Piercings: small sphere on ear/nose.
- Tattoos: small colored patches on arms (cylinders).

Let's implement with helper functions.

Species differences:
Goblin:
- skin green
- ears: two large cones on head sides
- nose: cone
- hunched: torso rotation.x=0.2, head forward
Rat:
- skin gray/brown
- ears: spheres
- snout: cylinder
- tail: curved tube at back

Let's write.

```js
function createCharacter(species, outfit) {
  const g = new THREE.Group();
  const skin = species === 'goblin' ? 0x4caf50 : 0x8d6e63;
  const skinMat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({color:skin, roughness:0.8});
  // torso
  const torso = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.32,0.42,0.9,12), skinMat);
  torso.position.y = 0.95;
  if (species==='goblin') torso.rotation.x = 0.2;
  g.add(torso);
  // head
  const head = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.3,16,16), skinMat);
  head.position.y = 1.62;
  if (species==='goblin') { head.position.z = 0.08; head.scale.set(1.05,0.9,1.05);}
  g.add(head);
  // neck
  const neck = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.12,0.14,0.18,8), skinMat);
  neck.position.y = 1.42; g.add(neck);
  // arms
  const armColor = outfit.tops ? outfit.tops.color : skin; // top covers? we'll keep skin arms maybe top sleeves? 
  ...
}
```

Actually clothing top should cover torso; arms skin. Pants cover legs. Socks cover lower legs. Shoes feet. Underwear maybe hip.

