Opponent species random.

Round setup:
```js
function startRound() {
  state.round++;
  state.theme = THEMES[Math.floor(Math.random()*THEMES.length)];
  state.options = {};
  for (const c of CATEGORIES) state.options[c.key] = pickOptions(ITEM_POOLS[c.key],5);
  state.playerOutfit = {};
  for (const c of CATEGORIES) state.playerOutfit[c.key] = state.options[c.key][0];
  // opponents choose
  for (const opp of state.opponents) {
    opp.outfit = {};
    for (const c of CATEGORIES) {
      opp.outfit[c.key] = bestChoice(state.theme, state.options[c.key]);
    }
  }
  state.selectedCategory = CATEGORIES[0].key;
  showDressing();
}
```

Scoring round:
```js
function finishRoundScoring() {
  const theme = state.theme;
  const playerScore = scoreOutfit(theme, state.playerOutfit);
  const oppScores = state.opponents.map(o=>({name:o.name, score:scoreOutfit(theme,o.outfit)}));
  // presentation bonus
  ...
  state.roundScores.push({theme, player:playerScore, opponents:oppScores});
  state.scores.player += playerScore;
  for (opp) state.scores[opp.name] += opp.score;
  showScores(playerScore, oppScores);
}
```

Need run runway before scoring. Flow: dressing -> click "Auf den Laufsteg" -> showRunway() animates -> then show scores.

Runway animation:
We need spawn characters sequentially. Use an async function with await delays. Since no sleep? We can use setTimeout Promise. Implement `wait(ms)`.

```js
function wait(ms){ return new Promise(res=>setTimeout(res,ms)); }
async function runRunway() {
  clearStageChars();
  // player first? 
  const candidates = [{name: state.playerName, species: state.playerSpecies, outfit: state.playerOutfit, isPlayer:true}, ...opponents];
  for (const cand of candidates) {
    // create char
    const char = createCharacter(cand.species, cand.outfit);
    char.position.set(0,0,-6);
    scene.add(char);
    state.activeChar = char;
    // walk to center
    await animateWalk(char, -6, 0, 2000);
    await wait(900);
    // pose: maybe rotate
    await animateWalk(char, 0, 6? no exit)
    // exit to side
    await animateExit(char, 1.5);
    scene.remove(char);
    // small delay
    await wait(300);
  }
  state.activeChar=null;
  finishRoundScoring();
}
```

Animate walk: tween position.z and slight bobbing. Need update in animation loop? Simpler use requestAnimationFrame within async. We'll implement tween function using rAF and resolve.

```js
function tween(obj, from, to, duration, update) {
  return new Promise(resolve=>{
    const start = performance.now();
    function step(now){
      const t = Math.min(1,(now-start)/duration);
      const eased = t<.5?2*t*t:-1+(4-2*t)*t; // ease
      update(eased);
      if (t<1) requestAnimationFrame(step); else resolve();
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(step);
  });
}
```

For walk:
```js
async function animateWalk(char, zFrom, zTo, duration) {
  await tween(char, zFrom, zTo, duration, (t)=>{
    char.position.z = zFrom + (zTo-zFrom)*t;
    char.position.y = Math.sin(t*Math.PI*4)*0.05; // bob
    // leg swing? skip
  });
}
```
Exit:
```js
async function animateExit(char, duration) {
  const startX = char.position.x;
  await tween(char, 0, 1, duration, t=>{
    char.position.x = startX + t*3;
    char.position.z += 0.02;
    char.rotation.y = t*0.8;
  });
}
```

Need also rotate character to face camera initially. Characters created facing +Z? Default cylinder faces camera? We'll set rotation.y = Math.PI (face camera) maybe. Let's set group.rotation.y = Math.PI so front faces camera (camera at +Z). Actually if walk from z=-6 to 0 (toward camera), character should face +Z. Default object faces +Z? A cylinder is symmetric; head no face details except species nose. We placed nose at +Z (position.z 0.32). So default faces +Z. Good. No rotation needed.

During walk from back to center, facing camera. Exit to side, rotate.

